A. THE WIDTH S: THE CANDIDATES, WHAT EACH GIVES FOR G = K_fan (n / d) / (4 pi S), WHAT REFUTES IT
   K_fan = 290, n / d = 1, H = 1 / 400 per interval; G in Links^3 per unit of content per interval^2
   16.2 (e) first: S = K (n / d) / (4 pi), G = 1 (natural units)                  S =       23.077  G = 1.000e+00   a choice of units: moves the number into h; alpha / alpha_G still rho_p^2, declared
   16.2 (e) second: S = sqrt 3 K (n / d) / (2 h), the unit the Planck mass        S =      251.147  G = 9.189e-02   refuted: alpha_G = M_p^2 >= 1 against 5.9 x 10^-39 (16.2 (e))
   16.2 (f): S = K_budget / 26, the budget unfixed                                S = (unfixed)      G = (unfixed)   derived under two assumptions; K_budget not fixed without hbar_law: no number
   the budget as the declared H: K_budget = H_den / H_num                         S =       15.385  G = 1.500e+00   moves the input from S to H; constant in time (H declared); nothing measured ties G to the declared H
   the budget as the Hubble length in Links: K_budget = c_0 / H                   S =        8.882  G = 2.598e+00   the same, and refuted if H is the running rate: G ~ H, Gdot / G = -H
   the budget as the Nodes within the Hubble length: K_budget = (4 pi / 3)(c_0 / H)^3 S =  1984327.510  G = 1.163e-05   the same, and refuted if H is the running rate: G ~ H^3, Gdot / G = -3 H

   the running rate under expansion-v1: a = 1 + H t gives the physical Hubble rate H / (1 + H t), falling as 1 / t under Milne;
   G ~ H: Gdot / G = -1 H_0 = -7.2e-11 per year against lunar laser ranging's 7.6e-14 per year (one sigma): refuted by a factor 942
   G ~ H^3: Gdot / G = -3 H_0 = -2.1e-10 per year against lunar laser ranging's 7.6e-14 per year (one sigma): refuted by a factor 2826
   the hierarchy alpha / alpha_G = rho_p^2 (3.4, 16.4) is untouched by every candidate: S sets the unit of G, the declared charge per unit of content carries the 10^36;
   what would make S = f(H) more than a relabelling: a rule driving the wall's rate H by the content (a Friedmann relation, 3 H^2 = 8 pi G rho), which the six verbs do not have; the wall's H is declared and the content does not move it

B. THE PUSH'S EUCLIDEAN DIVISIONS: IS THERE AN ACCELERATION FLOOR?
   (i) the push per column on main is by_clock(age, abs(V E n), D d): the whole part of the CUMULATIVE age x X / d, delivered as it crosses each integer;
       on gravity the divisor is 1 (3.5 item 7) and the push is exact per interval; on the branch acc_push keeps the remainder. A weak field on integers:
       X / d = 1 / 1000 per interval over 100000 intervals: the cumulative form delivers 100 (exact 100), a discarding floor would deliver 0
       X / d = 1 / 7 per interval over 100000 intervals: the cumulative form delivers 14285 (exact 14286), a discarding floor would deliver 0
       X / d = 3 / 5 per interval over 100000 intervals: the cumulative form delivers 60000 (exact 60000), a discarding floor would deliver 0
       the law's form loses nothing in the mean: the floor is zero, the granularity a delay of at most one push unit. A discarding floor is a remainder dropped, not one of the six (section 1's inventory).

   (ii) the shape a discarding floor would give, against the radial acceleration relation (the pin): a body at r from a source, Newton's a_N = G M / r^2 in push units;
        the floor: below half a unit nothing, at or above it one whole unit (a band); MOND's deep law a = sqrt(a_N a_0), the RAR's g_obs = g_bar / (1 - exp(-sqrt(g_bar / a_0)))
        r (Links) | a_N / a_0 | the floor's a | MOND's a | the floor's v^2 = r a | MOND's v^2
                2 |   25.0000 |       25.0000 |  25.1696 |                50.000 |     50.339
                5 |    4.0000 |        4.0000 |   4.6261 |                20.000 |     23.130
               10 |    1.0000 |        1.0000 |   1.5820 |                10.000 |     15.820
               14 |    0.5102 |        1.0000 |   0.9995 |                14.000 |     13.993
               20 |    0.2500 |        0.0000 |   0.6354 |                 0.000 |     12.707
               50 |    0.0400 |        0.0000 |   0.2207 |                 0.000 |     11.033
              100 |    0.0100 |        0.0000 |   0.1051 |                 0.000 |     10.508
        the floor's v^2 rises as r up to the radius where a_N falls below half a unit and is zero beyond: a band, never a flat curve (MOND's v^2 -> sqrt(G M a_0), constant);
        and the floor cuts the weak field where MOND raises it: the wrong sign of the departure before any number. The deep law is a root of the state, not one of the six (the vector test, record 202).

   (iii) the one discreteness of the far field the law does have: the fan's angular grain (3.2, 3.5 item 1, 15.5): a lone body reads a lone source only on one of its K lines;
         the fraction of a shell's Nodes on a line, K / N(r), N(r) -> 4 pi r^2:
         r =    10 Links, K =  290: 2.31e-01 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r =    10 Links, K = 1423: 1.00e+00 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r =   100 Links, K =  290: 2.31e-03 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r =   100 Links, K = 1423: 1.13e-02 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r =  1000 Links, K =  290: 2.31e-05 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r =  1000 Links, K = 1423: 1.13e-04 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r = 10000 Links, K =  290: 2.31e-07 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         r = 10000 Links, K = 1423: 1.13e-06 of the shell's Nodes read the source, the rest read 0; the shell mean is Newton's (Gauss exact)
         off the lines the far field is weaker than Newton's, never stronger: the departure has the wrong sign for a flat curve; a crowd of sources at many angles fills the lines (the shell mean per Node)

   (iv) the granular push against c H: one row of amount 1 per interval at a body gives a = 1 / S Links per interval^2 (3.3: a = push / (Q S M), push = M x u_d, u_d = Q); c H = H / sqrt 3;
        a_unit / (c H) = sqrt 3 H_den / (S H_num), dimensionless; nature's a_0 / (c H_0) = 1 / (2 pi) = 0.159 (Milgrom's coincidence):
        S =         1: a_unit / (c H) = 6.928e+02
        S =         8: a_unit / (c H) = 8.660e+01
        S =        32: a_unit / (c H) = 2.165e+01
        S =       512: a_unit / (c H) = 1.353e+00
        S =      4353: a_unit / (c H) = 1.592e-01
        S =     45120: a_unit / (c H) = 1.536e-02
        S =   1048576: a_unit / (c H) = 6.607e-04
        S = 268435456: a_unit / (c H) = 2.581e-06
        the S at which the granular push equals nature's a_0 at H = 1 / 400: 4353, a number no count of the structure carries (13.3: the widths sit at several budgets);
        under S = K_budget / 26 with K_budget = H_den / H_num: a_unit / (c H) = 45.0, against 0.159; and the floor is zero whatever S
        under S = K_budget / 26 with K_budget = c_0 / H in Links: a_unit / (c H) = 78.0, against 0.159; and the floor is zero whatever S
        in m / s^2: not computable, the dictionary's Link and interval are not fixed (16.2 (f), NATURE.md 'What needs the conversion'); c H_0 = 6.80e-10 m s^-2, c H_0 / (2 pi) = 1.08e-10 against a_0 = 1.2e-10

   (v) the register's small-r departures (series C item 5: count x r / q within 10 percent for r >= 8, the ring mean over mostly empty Nodes, one ray or none):
        the lattice's shell count N(r) and the fan's grain (3.2's table, r / N(r) exact), not a floor: the number that pins it is the ring reading r / N(r), 0.125 at r = 4, and it is Newton's

C. THE VERDICTS: (A) none derives S: the two of 16.2 (e) are a unit choice and a refuted one, the budget form leaves K_budget unfixed, and a budget tied to H moves the input (constant H) or is refuted by lunar laser ranging (running H);
   (B) REFUTED: the push's divisions keep the remainder (the floor is zero), a discarding floor would cut the weak field with a band shape (the wrong sign and the wrong shape against the RAR), and the deep law needs a root (not one of the six); the dark sector stays as record 283 says

D. THE FAR SYSTEM READ BEFORE ANY CLICK (record 285): DOES THE OFFERS' SPREAD SET A FLOOR ON THE READ VELOCITY?
   (1) what the detector reads of a stream is its arrival count per interval (the Doppler, section 2: the crossing rule) and the moments of the arriving rows (order 0, 1, 2 and the age);
       a spread of the rows' direction labels or phases changes the moments of order 1 and 2 and the phase-count vector's width, not the count per interval. On integers:
       label spread +- 0 steps, phase spread  0 steps: the arrival spacing over the release spacing 0.2500 = 1 - v / c at v / c = 3 / 4 (unchanged)
       label spread +- 3 steps, phase spread 16 steps: the arrival spacing over the release spacing 0.2500 = 1 - v / c at v / c = 3 / 4 (unchanged)
       label spread +-40 steps, phase spread 63 steps: the arrival spacing over the release spacing 0.2500 = 1 - v / c at v / c = 3 / 4 (unchanged)
       the read velocity is the count's, whatever the labels' and phases' spread: a spread broadens the line (order 2) and does not move its centre (order 1 in time)

   (2) what grows with the distance or the crowd met, so that a far system differs from the Sun: on main nothing but the age and the count's dilution (a row reads nothing of the crowd, 5.4);
       under meeting-v1 the direction label turns one step per N crowd units met and the phase gains the crowd met (section 5.4): the spread of the labels and of the phase-count vector grows with the crowd met, the count per interval does not

   (3) the pins against a floor on the read velocity from a spread:
       the Sun's planets read by the same detector, the radial-velocity precision: v = 0.001 km/s, beta = 3.3e-09
       a galaxy's edge, the flat speed: v = 200 km/s, beta = 6.7e-04
       a spread fixed at birth reads the same for the Sun and for a far galaxy: bounded by the planets' Doppler at 1 m/s (a part in 2 x 10^5 of a galaxy's edge);
       a spread growing with the distance is refuted by the Tully-Fisher relation's independence of distance: the flat speed follows M^(1/4) with 0.1 dex scatter in M (0.025 dex in v, 6 percent) from 1 to 100 Mpc, no term in d;
       M = 1e+08 M_sun: v_flat = (M / 47)^(1 / 4) =   38.2 km/s, the same at every distance
       M = 1e+09 M_sun: v_flat = (M / 47)^(1 / 4) =   67.9 km/s, the same at every distance
       M = 1e+10 M_sun: v_flat = (M / 47)^(1 / 4) =  120.8 km/s, the same at every distance
       M = 1e+11 M_sun: v_flat = (M / 47)^(1 / 4) =  214.8 km/s, the same at every distance
       the cluster's edge: Zwicky's dispersion is a spread of the CENTRES of many galaxies' lines (each galaxy its own source, its own count), which a width of each line cannot make;
       the Bullet Cluster: the bending under meeting-v1 is the crowd met along the path, unchanged by whether the rows clicked before; the offers' reading moves no lensing mass;
       the sky: a reading before the click repeats no source

   (4) VERDICT D: REFUTED: the read velocity is the arrival count, which no spread of labels or phases moves; a spread fixed at birth is bounded by the Solar System at a part in 2 x 10^5 of the edge speed, a spread growing with distance by Tully-Fisher's independence of distance; the cluster's dispersion is of centres, not widths

E. THE FIXED COMPUTATION K AT A GALAXY'S EDGE: THREE FORMS AGAINST THE RADIAL ACCELERATION RELATION AND TULLY-FISHER
   (1) the budget as a cap on the release at the source: a Node births at most K / 12 rows per interval (13.3, 12 operations per row born)
       K = 1.0e+04: at most 833 rows per interval per source Node
       K = 1.0e+06: at most 83333 rows per interval per source Node
       K = 9.4e+06: at most 783333 rows per interval per source Node
       the register's series C source releases 786432 rows per interval (q = 6 x 2^17), so a budget that is a law sits at K >= 9.4e+06; series 7's coefficients are linear in the source's content up to 2^24
       above the cap the far field is the same for every larger mass: v_flat^2 = r a with a = q_cap / (4 pi S r^2) x Q, so
       a source   1 times the cap: the far field x 1 (the cap's), v_flat x 1: the Tully-Fisher slope above the cap is infinite (nature's 4), and the field's shape stays 1 / r^2 (Keplerian, no flat part)
       a source  10 times the cap: the far field x 1 (the cap's), v_flat x 1: the Tully-Fisher slope above the cap is infinite (nature's 4), and the field's shape stays 1 / r^2 (Keplerian, no flat part)
       a source 100 times the cap: the far field x 1 (the cap's), v_flat x 1: the Tully-Fisher slope above the cap is infinite (nature's 4), and the field's shape stays 1 / r^2 (Keplerian, no flat part)
       and a galaxy is 10^11 source Nodes each under its own budget: the sum stays linear in their number; the cap acts on no galaxy, and where it acts it weakens the field (the wrong sign)

   (2) the budget as a cap on the forwarding at a dense Node: rows queued, none destroyed (the books' balance I5: released = in transit + absorbed + escaped, exact);
       in the steady state the flux through any closed surface is the release inside it (Gauss's law of the stream, 3.1, 5.5): the far field is Newton's; only the timing changes.
       at the edge the crowd against the budget (series E's presence k = 39.7 / r^2 rows per interval, q dwell / (4 pi) = 39.7):
       r =    10 Links: k = 3.97e-01 rows per interval; the budget spent on reading them, 26 k / K at K = 10^4: 1.0e-03 of an interval; the delay's gradient M / r^3 against Newton's M / r^2: 1.0e-01
       r =   100 Links: k = 3.97e-03 rows per interval; the budget spent on reading them, 26 k / K at K = 10^4: 1.0e-05 of an interval; the delay's gradient M / r^3 against Newton's M / r^2: 1.0e-02
       r =  1000 Links: k = 3.97e-05 rows per interval; the budget spent on reading them, 26 k / K at K = 10^4: 1.0e-07 of an interval; the delay's gradient M / r^3 against Newton's M / r^2: 1.0e-03
       nothing survives at the edge: the delay field (5.1) and the clock's suspension (5.2) act where the crowd is dense, and their gradient falls faster than Newton's

   (3) the suspension read as a floor at a sparse Node: the push is p += C a, bilinear in the coupling and the arriving flow, homogeneous of degree 1 in the rows (3.3, LAW.md section 3):
       a Node reading half the rows pushes half; no verb of the six adds to a push what is not in the rows (the constants of the law are rates and walls declared at load, none affine in the flow).
       if a floor were added by a comparison, a = max(a_N, a_floor) along the flow (verb D with a declared a_floor), what it gives against the pins:
       the Solar System: the Sun's pull at Saturn 6.5e-05 m s^-2, 5.4e+05 times a_0: the max form is silent there (Cassini's gamma - 1 = (2.1 +- 2.3) x 10^-5 untouched)
       r (Links) | a_N = 100 / r^2 | max(a_N, a_floor = 0.25) | v^2 = r a (the max form) | v^2 MOND (sqrt(a_N a_0), a_0 = 0.25)
              10 |          1.0000 |                   1.0000 |                    10.00 |      10.00
              20 |          0.2500 |                   0.2500 |                     5.00 |       5.00
              50 |          0.0400 |                   0.2500 |                    12.50 |       5.00
             100 |          0.0100 |                   0.2500 |                    25.00 |       5.00
             200 |          0.0025 |                   0.2500 |                    50.00 |       5.00
       the max form's v^2 rises as r beyond the onset: not flat, and v independent of M (the Tully-Fisher slope infinite); the flat curve needs a = sqrt(a_N a_0), a root: the seventh verb, and a declared a_0

   where K acts instead: at the centre, as the clock's suspension and the dwell (5.2, 13.2 (b)): series E's k_s r^2 = 41.5 and k_a r = 36.1, the clock at 1 / (1 + k n / d), the redshift M / r at first order

   VERDICT E: REFUTED per form: (1) the release cap weakens the far field where it acts, keeps the 1 / r^2 shape, gives an infinite Tully-Fisher slope and acts on no galaxy; (2) the forwarding cap conserves the flux (the books) and leaves Newton at the edge, only the centre's timing; (3) no verb makes a sparse Node push more than it reads, and a floor by comparison rises as r, not flat; the deep law needs a root
